    "The Addis Ababa Transmission and Distribution System Rehabilitation and Upgrading Project aims to enhance the power supply capability and reliability of the city’s electrical network. A feasibility study has proposed the construction of a new Addis Center Substation south of the African Union Headquarters, along with the reinforcement of Woregenu and Gofa substations.Key components of the proposed upgrades include:1.New Addis Center Substation:      oCapacity: 200 MVA (4×50MVA, 132/15kV power transformers)      oLayout: 3 transmission line bays, 1 single circuit to Black Lion substation via 132kV cable2.Transmission Line Upgrades:     oReplacement of Kaliti-I to Addis Center line with double circuit 132kV monopole line (9.1 km overhead + 4.3 km underground cable)     oTap connection to Gofa substation (0.2 km single circuit line)     oSingle circuit cable to Black Lion (225 MVA capacity)3.Substation Reinforcements:     oWoregenu: Additional 50MVA transformer and Line-In Line-Out (LILO) configuration with a new 3.5 km cable    o     Kaliti North Substation: LILO configuration replacing existing Kaliti-I to Bole Lemi TP lineThe technical study indicates that these reinforcements will significantly improve the power supply capacity and reliability across Addis Ababa and surrounding substations.Estimated Project Cost: 120.7 million USD": 1,
    "o Debrezeit III '- Hurso '- Ayisha Power Transmission Project (Ethiopia)- A major power sector initiative led by Ethiopian Electric Power (EEP), this two-year, USD 399.224 million project'-financed by the World Bank'-aims to improve transmission capacity and grid reliability in eastern Ethiopia. - The project is in its final feasibility phase, moving toward detailed routing and preliminary design.o Key Components:- Transmission Lines'- 355 km double-circuit 400 kV line: Debrezeit III → Hurso'- 198 km double-circuit 230 kV line: Hurso → Ayisha'- Alignments prioritize road access for maintainability, with ESIA and RAP to be finalized during route survey.- Substation Works'- Debre Zeit III:   o 400 kV double busbar extension   o 2-line bays for Hurso Lines 1 & 2'- Hurso (Upgrade): o 400 kV & 230 kV double busbar systems o 4 line bays (Ayisha + Debrezeit lines) o 2x 400/230 kV, 250 MVA autotransformers o 400 kV bus coupler bay o 3 switchable shunt reactors (2×60 MVAr, 1×135 MVAr)'- Ayisha (New Build): o 400 kV double busbar system o 2 line bays for Hurso Lines 1 & 2 o 1 bus coupler bay o Space for 4 future line bayso This project supports Ethiopia’s grid expansion strategy, integrating renewable energy sources while enhancing reliability and capacity.": 1,
    "2-Project DetailsDominican Republic Water Supply and Sanitation Sector Modernization ProgramThe program follows a Multiphase Programmatic Approach (MPA) with a total duration of 10 years (2023'-2032), divided into two main phases:■ Phase I (2023'-2027): Foundational and Pilot Phase- Objective:To implement key reforms, improve basic access to safe water and sanitation services, and initiate operational and institutional transformation in critical regions.-Main Components:1. PforR (Program-for-Results) '- USD 225 million'- Implemented by INAPA, CORAASAN, and CORAAVEGA.'- Focused on the Yaque del Norte river basin.'- Based on 10 DLIs (Disbursement Linked Indicators), independently verified.'- Expected results:- New safe water connections: 34,700 households.- New safe sanitation connections: 76,300 households.- Reduction in Non-Revenue Water (NRW).- Improvements in energy efficiency.2. IPF (Investment Project Financing) '- USD 25 million'- Executed by MEPyD and INDRHI.'- Focused on institutional strengthening, including:- Development of legal and regulatory frameworks.- Water rights registration systems.- Modernization of hydrometric systems and water resource planning.- Design of tariff regulatory frameworks.- Development of water monitoring and governance systems.-Strategic Goal:To establish the operational, technical, and legal foundations for deeper and more sustainable sectoral transformation in Phase II.-Current Status: As of April 2025, there are no specific announcements of new tenders currently open at INAPA. However, the project framework and program schedule suggest that upcoming calls for bids in these areas are expected:- Expansion of potable water distribution networks in other regions of the country.- Construction and rehabilitation of sanitation infrastructure, including treatment plants and sewerage systems.- Procurement of equipment and technologies to enhance operational efficiency and water resource management.________________________________________■ Phase II (2026'-2032): Scaling and Consolidation Phase- Objective:To consolidate and institutionalize water and sanitation sector reforms, expanding service coverage and sustainability at the national level.- Current Status:'- Not yet formally approved but planned as part of the MPA (The World Bank will assess Phase I performance before launching Phase II).'- Estimated start: June 2026.- Expected Areas of Focus:'- National expansion to other regions facing water stress or low service coverage.'- Modernization of major infrastructure, including advanced water treatment plants and expanded distribution networks.'- Strengthening the national water regulator and consolidating a national sanitation entity.'- Tariff and financial sustainability: Implementing cost-recovery mechanisms.'- Potential inclusion of climate resilience instruments, renewable energy solutions, and digital technologies (e.g., sensors, remote monitoring systems).- Financing:'- An additional USD 250 million loan is anticipated.'- The mixed financing model (PforR + IPF) will be maintained.'- Lessons learned from Phase I will be applied to new regions and stakeholders.● SourcesWorld Bank: https://documents.worldbank.org/en/publication/documents-reports/documentdetail/099164503072314540INAPA: https://wp.inapa.gob.do/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Estrategia-provisional-Eficiencia-Energetica-df.pdf": 1,
    "o 빈그룹 발주의 풍력발전 프로젝트o Background:-Under the implementation plan of the National Power Development Plan for the period 2021'-2030, with a vision to 2050, 13 wind power projects with a total capacity of 872.5 MW have been approved for Tra Vinh province.-In the future, Tra Vinh province still has high potential to develop renewable energy with the total capacity of more than 26,000 MW, especially near shore and off shore wind power.o Project details:-The total land use area of the project: 13,400 ha-Capacity: 3,000 MW, divided into 2 phases+ Phase 1: 1,500 MW+ Phase 2: 1,500 MW-Number of turbines each phase: 190-250 (6MW~8MW turbine)-Turbine height: 140 mWhen it comes into operation, this plant is expected to generate about 9 billion kWh/year which is equivalent to the power generation of LNG Nhon Trach 3-Nhon Trach 4 plant.": 1,
    "-본 프로젝트는 수처리 정화시설 프로젝트로, 하이랑 및 꽝찌성 인근에 수도를 보급하는 시설 설립 프로젝트. 꽝찌성 관계자를 통해 프로젝트 정보 수집-The project is to build a clean water plant with a capacity of 150,000m3/day-night. This is a large-scale centralized clean water supply project, serving as a water source for the inter-regional water supply system (Hai Lang-Quang Tri Commune-Trieu Phong-Dong Ha City-Gio Linh-Vinh Linh). -Tentative area: 90 ha-The plant is included a clean water supply pipeline system pumping stations; water supply rehydration canal and a system of equipment and machinery for operation. Specific technical specification would be proposed by investors.": 1,
    "뉴 무라바(New Murabba) 물 공급 시스템 인프라 공사사우디 국부펀드(PIF)가 전액 출자한 뉴 무라바 개발회사(New Murabba Development Company, NMDC)는 리야드에 세계 최대 규모의 현대식 도심 개발 프로젝트인 뉴 무라바(New Murabba) 프로젝트의 일환으로 물 공급 시스템 인프라 공사를 추진할 계획4억 달러 규모의 본 프로젝트는 다음과 같은 내용을 포함- 일 처리용량 160,000m³의 물 공급 시스템 건설- 저장 탱크 건설- 펌핑 스테이션 건설- 슬러지 처리 시설 건설- 배급 센터 건설- 수도 계량기 설치- 송수관 매설- 기타 관련 시설 건설": 1
